process-stale-sends.m on the machine's GPU, where the sends go directly
through the receivers' queues: in 300 rounds, no fresh process gets a word
of the sender to the ended process before it in its slot, and none of the
words, nor their blocks, is left once the processes end.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-stale-sends.m -o %t
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 120 %t gpu 300 20000 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines
CHECK:rounds 300, stale words got 0, in 0 rounds
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 blocks of messages between GPU processes are allocated
